 "notes": "Shelf \"Pour-over & manual brewers\" rebuilt: 9 kinds (2 carried over: French press k62, Moka pot k65 with old \"s\" kept; 7 new), 24 archetypes, 16 brands, 1 tradition. Old Moka pot models (Moka Express, Venus) became versions of the Moka Express archetype. All archetype/brand/tradition sources were retrieved this session (Wikipedia pages, Hario/Bialetti/Alessi/Kinto/Origami/Soy/AeroPress/Espro/Kalita maker pages, UNESCO decision 8.COM 8.28, Sprudge/PDG/Today/DCN/Belco articles). Hario dates V60 to 2005 (its own history page) rather than the brief's 2004. Years left blank where no retrieved page confirmed them (Kalita Wave launch, Bodum Chambord launch, Fellow Stagg [X], Brikka, Origami brand founding, Soy founding, Fellow/Abid founding). December Dripper has mk \"\" because no page naming its manufacturing company was retrieved (designers Nick Cho and Youngmin Lee are in d). Omitted: Hario Drip Decanter, Bodum Kenya/Brazil presses, De'Longhi/Giannini moka pots, Walküre/Bee House drippers, Bosnian džezva as separate archetype, Arabic dallah (serving pot, belongs with tableware) — none attested on a retrieved page beyond a passing mention. Trade/commercial items (Toddy 5-gallon commercial, Hario commercial syphons) left out per scope rule. Filter paper kept as a detail/type under Pour-over dripper, not a kind.",
